        "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Portraius Studio: the Image studio\n\n**With a cast (top row).** The \"Film still\" preset with Walt as {lead}. The prompt is the app's compiler output: which image is whose, a lock on the face, the scene, the camera, then skin and lens realism. Put a character's sheet and front view in `ComfyUI/input/` as `walt-sheet.jpg` and `walt-front.jpg`: unzip any `.portraius` file, they're `sheet/turnaround.png` and `sheet/front.png`. The samples are in this repo's `public/samples/`.\n\n**Editing an image (bottom row).** The source goes first, then the cast's references, and the prompt numbers them the same way. Put the image to edit in as `walt-diner.jpg` and an element's sheet as `satchel-sheet.jpg` (both in `public/samples/`).\n\nThe app scores each still against the character and retries once under 60; the graph doesn't. Settings are the Image studio's defaults: 2K, Best. Needs a Comfy account with credits: these are partner nodes."
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## Portraius Studio: the Image studio\n\n**With a cast (top row).** The \"Film still\" preset with Walt as {lead}. The prompt is the app's compiler output: which image is whose, a lock on the face, the scene, the camera, then skin and lens realism. Put a character's sheet and front view in `ComfyUI/input/` as `walt-sheet.jpg` and `walt-front.jpg`: unzip any `.portraius` file, they're `sheet/turnaround.png` and `sheet/front.png`. The samples are in this repo's `public/samples/`.\n\n**Editing an image (bottom row).** The source goes first, then the cast's references, and the prompt numbers them the same way. Put the image to edit in as `walt-diner.jpg` and an element's sheet as `satchel-sheet.jpg` (both in `public/samples/`).\n\nThe app scores each still against the character and retries once under 60; the graph doesn't. Settings are the Image studio's defaults: 2K, Best. Needs a Comfy account with credits: these are partner nodes."
      }
    },
